{
 "source": {
  "photo": "1958-Gibson-ES-225T-1.webp (studio photo, sunburst ES-225T), supplied by the project owner. The ES-225T and ES-295 share this outline.",
  "listing": "Gibson ES-225/1958 ES-225TD/info.txt: 24.75in scale, neck-body joint at the 14th fret, 20 frets, 16.25in wide, 1-15/16in deep, single-bound top and back, unbound F-holes.",
  "method": "Pixel trace of a straight-on studio photo (1707 x 2560), not a plan. Scale: the 20 fret lines along the neck were fitted against 24.75in equal-temperament positions (1.847 px/mm at the neck plane, residuals up to +-5 px because of lens and perspective); the body sits nearer the camera, so body-plane features use 1.918 px/mm, which is what makes the body 16.25in wide as the 1958 ES-225TD listing says. The outline is the binding line (bright against the black backdrop), flood-filled from outside, closed with a wall along the bass-side neck junction (display y=925) and down the fingerboard's treble edge (x=727), opened to drop spurs, eroded 2 px to the line centre, the tailpiece bump flattened to a parabola, smoothed and fitted with cubic Beziers (0.45 mm). Treble side is +X, Y=0 is the junction line, X=0 the body's own centreline (display x=662; the neck axis sits at 668.5, a 3 mm parallax between planes). The F-hole is the bass one thresholded out of the photo and mirrored; the pickguard is the black plastic region, dilated to its white binding.",
  "accuracy": "Outline about +-2 mm; hardware positions about +-3 mm; Y positions carry the photo's perspective. A first draft to refine by hand."
 },
 "measured": {
  "nutToBodyEdgeMm": 348.6183,
  "nutToBodyEdgeNote": "Fret 14. The owner said fret 15 (364.4), but the photo puts the body/fingerboard junction between frets 14 and 15 (fret 14.3 at the neck-plane scale, 13.6 at the body-plane scale) and the listing says the 14th; with fret 14 the trapeze bridge lands 2 mm from where the photo has it, with fret 15 it would be 18 mm off.",
  "fingerboardOverhangMm": 103.6228,
  "bridgePhotoYMm": 282.1,
  "bodyThicknessMm": 42.0,
  "bodyThicknessNote": "An assumption. The listing gives 1-15/16in (49.2 mm) depth for the fully hollow original; this is the core below the rim of a carved_cap, in the same proportion as the ES-335 draft.",
  "fHoleDepthMm": 20
 },
